WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.633
A newly released

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:01.501
review

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.303
by the US State Department claims

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:04.604
that the Biden administration

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:06.172
bungled several

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:07.574
aspects of the American withdrawal

00:00:07.574 --> 00:00:08.875
from Afghanistan in August.

00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:10.310
2021 CNN

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:11.611
national security correspondent

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:12.645
Kyla Abbott is live

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:13.513
for us from the State Department.

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:14.280
And highly

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.715
unlike the White House

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:17.083
report released yesterday,

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:18.218
this separate

00:00:18.218 --> 00:00:19.052
State Department

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:21.721
review identifies several clear missteps

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:23.189
from the Biden administration

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:24.624
that contributed to the chaotic

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:26.693
and deadly withdrawal. Tell us more.

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:27.360
Yeah, that's right.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.728
So according to our sources,

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:30.497
Jake this State Department

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:31.231
after action

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:31.931
report

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:35.068
has far more findings and recommendations

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:35.335
in it

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:36.236
than the document

00:00:36.236 --> 00:00:37.871
that was put out yesterday

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:39.105
from the White House.

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:39.973
And according

00:00:39.973 --> 00:00:40.707
to our sources

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:42.842
who have either seen this report

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:44.611
or have been described the report,

00:00:44.611 --> 00:00:46.379
they say that there are 34

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:48.048
recommendations in total

00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:49.482
and they're very specific.

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:51.551
They talk about doing things

00:00:51.651 --> 00:00:53.787
such as putting a single official

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:54.654
in charge

00:00:54.654 --> 00:00:55.755
when there are the complex

00:00:55.755 --> 00:00:56.923
crisis situations

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:57.357
like this

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:59.059
or standing up a red team

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:00.860
to challenge assumptions

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:01.694
that are being made.

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:02.362
These are things

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:04.397
that the Biden administration did not do

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:06.266
during the Afghanistan withdrawal

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:07.367
and recommendations

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:09.369
for how it could have gone better now.

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:11.638
In contrast, that White House document

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:13.840
that was put out yesterday

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.542
does cite some lessons

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:16.276
learned, such

00:01:16.276 --> 00:01:19.079
as prioritizing earlier evacuations.

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:20.647
But what it really does

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:22.515
is dwells on the decisions

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:22.982
that were made

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:24.918
during the Trump administration

00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:26.619
and says that those decisions

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:28.621
that were made, such as striking a deal

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:29.622
with the Taliban

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:31.357
to get out the US

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:32.792
completely from the country,

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:33.693
drawing down U.S.

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:34.861
troops in the country,

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:36.763
severely constrained

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:39.299
what President Biden was able to do.

00:01:39.466 --> 00:01:40.900
And so there is a disconnect

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:42.068
between these two reports.

00:01:42.068 --> 00:01:43.770
The NSC is saying

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:46.306
that they are simply separate reports

00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:48.842
that the one from the White House

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:51.311
was drawing on certain parts

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:52.412
of the State Department report,

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:53.880
but it wasn't mirroring it.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.081
What are you hearing from

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:56.049
members of Congress

00:01:56.049 --> 00:01:56.850
and diplomats

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:59.119
about the White House report?

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:00.820
Yeah, so members of Congress,

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.055
particularly Republicans,

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:03.423
are being very critical of what

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:05.058
the White House put out yesterday.

00:02:05.058 --> 00:02:06.192
Congressman McCaul,

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:07.227
who is leading

00:02:07.227 --> 00:02:09.129
the investigation into the Biden

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:10.096
administration withdrawal

00:02:10.096 --> 00:02:11.264
from Afghanistan,

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:11.831
saying, quote,

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:13.933
that it was a brazen whitewashing

00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:15.869
of their failure in Afghanistan,

00:02:15.869 --> 00:02:17.303
calling it disgraceful

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:19.606
unjust and flat-Out insulting.

00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:20.840
And then we talk to diplomats

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:21.441
in this building

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:23.943
who frankly are more interested in seeing

00:02:24.144 --> 00:02:25.411
what the State Department's

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:27.780
report findings actually are,

00:02:28.014 --> 00:02:29.249
because those haven't been made

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:30.216
public yet, Jake.

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:32.118
And our understanding is that even though

00:02:32.118 --> 00:02:33.553
parts of this report

00:02:33.553 --> 00:02:35.455
were largely classified,

00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:36.890
the findings themselves were not.

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:37.891
But the State Department

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:39.959
still has yet to release those widely

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:41.261
except for sending it to Congress

00:02:41.261 --> 00:02:42.262
yesterday Jake.

00:02:42.262 --> 00:02:42.462
All right.

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:43.530
Candidate Kylie

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:44.430
Atwood at the State Department,

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:45.265
thanks so much.

00:02:45.265 --> 00:02:46.099
Let's bring in former

00:02:46.099 --> 00:02:47.267
Republican Congressman

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:48.501
Peter Meyer of Michigan.

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:49.536
He's a former sergeant

00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:50.403
in the Army Reserves.

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:51.571
He served in Iraq.

00:02:51.571 --> 00:02:53.373
He also spent some time in Afghanistan

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:54.774
as a civilian aid worker.

00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:57.243
And as we covered in August 20, 21,

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:58.978
he secretly flew to Kabul

00:02:58.978 --> 00:02:59.979
during the frenzied U.S.

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:01.381
evacuation back then

00:03:01.381 --> 00:03:02.982
with Congressman Seth Moulton.

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:04.117
Congressman, good to see you.

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:05.652
So you call the White House

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:07.520
report on withdrawal.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:08.521
You call it shameful.

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:10.757
You call it a craven whitewash of events.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:11.391
Tell us why

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:15.328
Oh, it's a political document,

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:16.462
plain and simple.

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:17.764
This was the

00:03:17.764 --> 00:03:19.165
Biden administration's attempt

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:20.066
to basically shift

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:21.701
blame back onto the Trump

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:23.269
administration for what happened

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:25.405
under the Biden administration's watch.

00:03:25.405 --> 00:03:27.540
In response to the hearings

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.309
that are taking place on Capitol Hill,

00:03:29.309 --> 00:03:30.944
with the now Republican majority

00:03:30.944 --> 00:03:32.545
finally scrutinizing

00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:34.581
the withdrawal operation,

00:03:34.581 --> 00:03:35.515
I mean, that was

00:03:35.515 --> 00:03:37.750
I served in 117th Congress

00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:40.186
while this was occurring,

00:03:40.186 --> 00:03:42.455
and the Democratic majority refused

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:43.423
to probe

00:03:43.423 --> 00:03:43.856
deeply,

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:45.725
refused to ask the tough questions

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:46.693
of the State Department

00:03:46.693 --> 00:03:47.460
of the Biden

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:48.528
administration in terms

00:03:48.528 --> 00:03:49.729
of how this withdrawal

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:51.898
went so catastrophically wrong.

00:03:51.898 --> 00:03:53.099
And finally,

00:03:53.099 --> 00:03:54.734
there are those questions being asked.

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:55.668
And the White House felt

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:56.669
they needed to respond.

00:03:56.669 --> 00:03:59.038
And they put this report out as a

00:03:59.038 --> 00:03:59.906
political document

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:00.673
and nothing more

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:03.209
without letting the Biden administration

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:04.010
off the hook in any way.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:04.811
Do you agree

00:04:04.811 --> 00:04:07.046
that the Trump administration,

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:08.081
you know, in negotiating

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:09.482
with the Taliban, did

00:04:09.482 --> 00:04:11.251
constrain the Biden administration

00:04:11.251 --> 00:04:12.885
to a degree in terms of

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:14.554
the withdrawal being mandated

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:18.691
Well, if you remember, under

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:19.592
the Doha agreement

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:20.760
that the Trump administration

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:22.262
signed with the Taliban,

00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:23.329
it initially had a May

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:25.365
20, 21 withdrawal date.

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:27.166
The Biden administration coming in,

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:28.067
and it should be remembered

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:29.068
that President Biden,

00:04:29.068 --> 00:04:30.903
as a campaign pledge

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:32.939
similar to President Trump,

00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:34.340
vowed to get our troops

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:35.875
out of Afghanistan. Right.

00:04:35.875 --> 00:04:37.310
So he may have been constrained

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:38.244
by the troop numbers.

00:04:38.244 --> 00:04:39.712
There were 2500 American

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:41.314
service members in country

00:04:41.314 --> 00:04:41.981
by the time

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:43.983
the Biden administration took office,

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:46.753
but he changed the deadline from May 1st

00:04:46.753 --> 00:04:48.421
to September the 11th

00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:50.223
and then realized the political optics of

00:04:50.223 --> 00:04:50.923
that were bad.

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:53.459
So moved it back to August 31st.

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:56.496
But frankly, again, I'm not going to say

00:04:56.496 --> 00:04:57.664
that the Trump administration

00:04:57.664 --> 00:04:58.931
set the Biden administration

00:04:58.931 --> 00:05:00.400
up for success,

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:01.734
but the Biden administration

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:03.436
executed the withdrawal

00:05:03.436 --> 00:05:05.505
and happened on their watch

00:05:05.505 --> 00:05:06.839
And the fact that nobody

00:05:06.839 --> 00:05:07.940
in this administration

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:09.676
takes responsibility for it,

00:05:09.676 --> 00:05:10.209
there has been

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:13.513
no one who has resigned or suffered

00:05:13.513 --> 00:05:15.415
any negative consequences

00:05:15.415 --> 00:05:18.151
from a career standpoint because of this.

00:05:18.151 --> 00:05:18.918
It's shameful.

00:05:18.918 --> 00:05:19.819
That hasn't been the case

00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:21.387
in other NATO countries,

00:05:21.387 --> 00:05:22.488
and it just shows

00:05:22.488 --> 00:05:23.489
how desperately

00:05:23.489 --> 00:05:24.257
this administration

00:05:24.257 --> 00:05:25.892
wants to leave Afghanistan

00:05:25.892 --> 00:05:26.893
in the rearview mirror.

00:05:26.893 --> 00:05:30.630
National security spokesman Admiral Kirby

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:31.964
took issue

00:05:31.964 --> 00:05:33.099
with the

00:05:33.099 --> 00:05:35.635
description of the withdrawal as chaotic.

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:38.504
But as it was happening,

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:40.473
he didn't have an issue with it.

00:05:40.473 --> 00:05:41.541
With that description,

00:05:41.541 --> 00:05:43.776
I want you to listen to him in 20, 21

00:05:44.043 --> 00:05:45.211
follow Ed by what

00:05:45.211 --> 00:05:46.579
he told reporters yesterday

00:05:48.581 --> 00:05:50.883
The crowd size is smaller

00:05:51.617 --> 00:05:54.120
now than it was in those first few days.

00:05:55.021 --> 00:05:57.790
And and so we're not experiencing

00:05:58.157 --> 00:06:00.393
to the degree we did last Monday

00:06:01.527 --> 00:06:04.630
the physical crush and chaos

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:06.399
for all this talk of chaos.

00:06:06.399 --> 00:06:09.035
I just didn't see it. Not from my perch.

00:06:09.035 --> 00:06:10.770
So, I mean, he did acknowledge

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:12.739
seeing the chaos that we all saw,

00:06:12.739 --> 00:06:15.341
you know, babies being lifted into the

00:06:15.341 --> 00:06:16.442
airport grounds.

00:06:16.442 --> 00:06:17.510
The people running

00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:19.979
clinging to the plane, etc., etc..

00:06:19.979 --> 00:06:21.514
The 13 service members

00:06:21.514 --> 00:06:23.683
killed by the suicide bomber

00:06:23.683 --> 00:06:25.351
in August 2021.

00:06:25.351 --> 00:06:27.153
And then yesterday

00:06:27.153 --> 00:06:27.720
he said

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:29.856
he didn't see chaos from his perspective.

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:33.493
What was your reaction to that?

00:06:35.395 --> 00:06:37.063
Astonishment

00:06:37.163 --> 00:06:39.232
at just a loss of words.

00:06:39.265 --> 00:06:42.468
I mean, this was a very well-documented,

00:06:43.169 --> 00:06:45.538
horrific chaotic moment.

00:06:45.805 --> 00:06:47.373
Now, when it came to what

00:06:47.373 --> 00:06:48.307
our men and women on

00:06:48.307 --> 00:06:49.208
the ground were doing,

00:06:49.208 --> 00:06:51.010
they were incredibly,

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:52.111
incredibly heroic

00:06:52.111 --> 00:06:53.646
and dedicated to the mission

00:06:53.646 --> 00:06:55.882
that they were forced into.

00:06:55.882 --> 00:06:57.583
But they tried to make order

00:06:57.583 --> 00:06:58.718
out of the chaos that was there,

00:06:58.718 --> 00:07:00.720
but denying that there was chaos.

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:02.188
I mean, it's equivalent to telling us

00:07:02.188 --> 00:07:04.557
to not believe are lying eyes.

00:07:04.557 --> 00:07:05.258
I mean,

00:07:05.291 --> 00:07:07.493
and I'm grateful that journalists,

00:07:07.493 --> 00:07:08.828
not only because of the footage

00:07:08.828 --> 00:07:09.562
that was coming out,

00:07:09.562 --> 00:07:09.996
but also

00:07:09.996 --> 00:07:11.431
because many journalists

00:07:11.431 --> 00:07:13.599
had either worked in Afghanistan

00:07:13.599 --> 00:07:15.368
or had friends and colleagues

00:07:15.368 --> 00:07:16.936
who were still there, fixers,

00:07:16.936 --> 00:07:17.170
you know,

00:07:17.170 --> 00:07:19.372
folks on the ground, local journalists,

00:07:19.372 --> 00:07:21.107
you know, they know the truth.

00:07:21.107 --> 00:07:23.342
The American public have seen the truth.

00:07:23.342 --> 00:07:24.610
But now this is an attempt

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:27.847
to basically revise history

00:07:28.047 --> 00:07:29.482
and pretend it was anything

00:07:29.482 --> 00:07:31.184
other than what it was. And I

00:07:33.252 --> 00:07:35.221
I'm just at a loss for words.

00:07:35.221 --> 00:07:35.621
Yeah.

00:07:35.621 --> 00:07:37.223
Former Republican Congressman

00:07:37.223 --> 00:07:39.292
Peter Meyer of Michigan,

00:07:39.292 --> 00:07:39.959
thank you so much.

00:07:39.959 --> 00:07:40.827
Always good to see you, sir.

